1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,310
In 539 BCE,

2
00:00:02,340 --> 00:00:05,450
Cyrus the Great turned his attention
to Babylon,

3
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:08,200
one of the ancient world's
greatest cities.

4
00:00:08,650 --> 00:00:10,820
After the Persian
victory at Opis,

5
00:00:10,870 --> 00:00:13,410
Babylon came under
Persian control.

6
00:00:14,110 --> 00:00:16,350
Ancient accounts describe
the city's capture

7
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:19,480
with little resistance,
though details differ.

8
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:21,560
Cyrus entered Babylon

9
00:00:21,590 --> 00:00:24,320
and presented himself
as a legitimate king,

10
00:00:24,450 --> 00:00:27,620
honoring local traditions
and the god Marduk.

11
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:31,480
The famous Cyrus Cylinder
records his royal claims

12
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:33,680
and his restoration
of religious sites

13
00:00:33,710 --> 00:00:35,480
and displaced communities.

14
00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:38,270
It is an extraordinary
artifact,

15
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:41,360
but not a modern declaration
of human rights.

16
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,490
Babylon became part
of a vast Persian Empire.

17
00:00:45,770 --> 00:00:48,090
More than twenty-five
centuries later,

18
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:50,660
the story of Cyrus
still raises questions

19
00:00:50,690 --> 00:00:52,760
about power, conquest,

20
00:00:52,830 --> 00:00:55,340
and how rulers wish
to be remembered.

